If conc. decreases from $0.8 \frac{\mathrm{mol}}{\mathrm{dm}^3}$ to $0.2 \frac{\mathrm{mol}}{\mathrm{dm}^3}$ it means $75 \%$ of reactant is consumed

\begin{aligned}
& \therefore \mathrm{t}_{75 \%}=2 \times \mathrm{t}_{1 / 2} \\
& \text { or } \mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}=6 \mathrm{hr}
\end{aligned}
